> factor x^6 - 1
factor x^6 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + x + 1)*(x^2 - x + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor x^4 - 1
factor x^4 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor x^2 + 5x + 6
factor x^2 + 5x + 6
  = (x + 2)*(x + 3)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor 2x^2 + 5x - 12
factor 2x^2 + 5x - 12
  = (2x - 3)*(x + 4)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor x^3 - 3x^2 + 3x - 1
factor x^3 - 3x^2 + 3x - 1
  = (x - 1)^3
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor 6x^4 + x^3 - 7x^2 - x + 1
factor 6x^4 + x^3 - 7x^2 - x + 1
  = (x - 1)*(3x - 1)*(x + 1)*(2x + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
